===== Critical structural fact: sf(e_3-e_1), sf(e_3-e_2) are NOT always 1 =====
Indeed: e_3 - e_1 = 0 - (-q^2) = q^2 in Q, sf = 1 (trivially squarefree as a square).
        e_3 - e_2 = 0 - (-1) = 1, sf = 1.
So sf(e_3-e_1) = sf(e_3-e_2) = 1 always.
The ONLY non-trivial root difference is sf(e_2 - e_1) = sf(q^2 - 1) = sf(P*Q)/(2mn squared) = sf(P)*sf(Q).

===== Predicted Selmer dimension: 2 + ω(sf(P)) + ω(sf(Q)) (modulo correlations) =====
Heuristic: each prime p | sf(P*Q) gives at most 1 F_2 generator
(plus 2 torsion dimensions for E[2](Q) = (Z/2)^2)

